<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* Named explicitly, and a real file: without one every browser asks for
       /favicon.ico on every page, which the sign-in guard answers with a
       redirect and the log records forever as noise. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="DmarcMonitor.Web.styles.css" />
    @* Before the stylesheet paints, not after. A person who chose dark and
       then sees a white page on every navigation has been given a flicker
       rather than a preference. Inline and synchronous for the same reason:
       a deferred script runs too late to prevent it.

       Wrapped because localStorage throws outright in some privacy modes,
       and a theme preference is not worth a blank page. *@
    <script>
        try {
            if (localStorage.getItem('dmarc-theme') === 'dark') {
                document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'dark';
            }
        } catch (e) { /* no stored preference is reachable; light is the default */ }
    </script>
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes />
    <script src="theme.js"></script>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
